        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I couldn’t answer quantitatively because MedCP’s clinical DB connection failed:\n\n`Adaptive Server connection failed (QCDIDDWDB001.ucsfmedicalcenter.org)`\n\nI also found no MedCP resources/schema exposed through the resource interface, and the local curated KB search did not return antimicrobial-resistance KG entries for this question.\n\nWhat I would compute once the connection is restored:\n\n- Identify antimicrobial classes flagged as high-resistance-signal in the KG.\n- Query local prescribing/orders by antimicrobial class.\n- For each index prescription, count whether a treatment-change code/order occurs within 7 days.\n- Report:\n  - class\n  - number of prescriptions\n  - share of all antimicrobial prescriptions\n  - number with treatment change ≤7 days\n  - treatment-change rate\n\nSo the current answer is: blocked by unavailable MedCP database connection; no reliable class ranking or 7-day change frequency can be produced from the available tools."
        }
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "userVisible": true,
        "agentVisible": true
